WEBVTT

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.331
The Irresponsible Captain
Tylor

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.970
We may be off the maps...
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.029
...but let's stay on this voyage.
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:14.873 --> 00:00:19.003
I will be holding, never let you go.

00:00:20.579 --> 00:00:23.415
Whatever we may want...
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:23.415 --> 00:00:25.542
...we'll take as we need.
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:26.318 --> 00:00:30.345
So let's just go wherever we please!
Omoi no Mama Yukou!

00:00:32.057 --> 00:00:34.826
Make me your partner...
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:34.826 --> 00:00:37.454
...on this journey.
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:37.729 --> 00:00:41.324
One that you trust more than words!
Michizure ni Shite

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:47.431
Come on now and sail away for future!
Imasugu sail away for future

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.941
Things are waiting...
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:49.941 --> 00:00:53.138
...that we've never seen before!
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:57.148
Just take your cares...
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:00:57.148 --> 00:01:01.209
...and throw them all away.
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:01:01.453 --> 00:01:06.083
Come together, just think of tomorrow.

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:09.349
Let's go!

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:15.988
EQUATION OF KINDNESS

00:01:36.688 --> 00:01:39.088
Christ, I'm amazed we're still alive.

00:01:39.157 --> 00:01:41.455
Guess there really is such
a thing as dumb luck!

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:47.696
Idiot! Dumb luck like his
is luck we don't need!

00:01:47.832 --> 00:01:50.164
Hey, guys! Working hard?

00:01:50.769 --> 00:01:51.667
Captain!

00:01:53.171 --> 00:01:57.505
Fix her up good!
The Soyokaze's our home, too.

00:01:59.177 --> 00:02:00.974
You're the one who wrecked it!

00:02:01.313 --> 00:02:03.014
Once you finish with the outside...

00:02:03.014 --> 00:02:05.482
...the engine room needs work.
Do a good job!

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.580
He's the type who never
gets discouraged by anything.

00:02:19.764 --> 00:02:23.029
Dom, you haven't forgotten
my orders, have you?

00:02:23.201 --> 00:02:25.533
No, Highness. Fear not.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:30.239
I've positioned a secret agent
very near to Tylor.

00:02:30.875 --> 00:02:33.537
I hold no blame for you in
any of what's happened.

00:02:34.212 --> 00:02:36.476
But now he's even managed to kill Donan.

00:02:36.648 --> 00:02:38.775
Doesn't that make this situation more serious?

00:02:38.983 --> 00:02:41.417
As you say. Because of that...

00:02:41.553 --> 00:02:45.819
...I must proceed cautiously
to carry out your orders.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.858
Tylor isn't one who'd let his guard down.

00:02:49.894 --> 00:02:53.660
He's made a man given to quick
decisions move cautiously.

00:02:54.132 --> 00:02:56.100
You want him as much as I do.

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:57.630
Yes.

00:02:58.436 --> 00:03:00.063
I've had to wait this long already.

00:03:00.338 --> 00:03:03.273
I look forward to your
bringing him to me alive.

00:03:03.575 --> 00:03:04.337
Your Excellency.

00:03:05.777 --> 00:03:06.766
Shia Has.

00:03:07.245 --> 00:03:09.543
It's time to make our move.

00:03:10.915 --> 00:03:13.679
Let us avenge Admiral Donan.

00:03:13.918 --> 00:03:15.852
I'll leave the exact method to your discretion...

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.181
...but be sure to bring Tylor to me alive.

00:03:18.256 --> 00:03:21.623
That is Her Highness' wish. Bear it in mind.

00:03:21.793 --> 00:03:22.851
Don't worry.

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:32.058
Tylor... We shall meet once more.

00:03:35.774 --> 00:03:38.868
For meritorious action in
destroying the Donan fleet...

00:03:38.943 --> 00:03:42.379
...you are to receive the United
Planets Order of Merit...

00:03:42.447 --> 00:03:44.347
...first class on the carrier Ho-Oh.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:47.886
It's a direct message from Admiral Mifune.

00:03:47.886 --> 00:03:49.217
A medal, huh?

00:03:49.954 --> 00:03:51.387
We're honored, sir!

00:03:54.225 --> 00:03:56.557
I'll be waiting, Captain Tylor.

00:04:00.965 --> 00:04:04.298
I'm tired from inspecting
the hull repair work.

00:04:04.636 --> 00:04:07.036
You can get the medal for me, Yuriko.

00:04:07.572 --> 00:04:10.769
Take a look at what you were
just out inspecting!

00:04:11.209 --> 00:04:13.200
The man who let a ship get so damaged...

00:04:13.278 --> 00:04:15.109
...doesn't deserve leave or a medal!

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.872
We can't even use our main guns!

00:04:17.315 --> 00:04:20.910
But, Commander, the fact remains
that we destroyed the Donan fleet.

00:04:20.985 --> 00:04:23.419
As soldiers, I believe that it's only right...

00:04:23.488 --> 00:04:26.048
...that we be honored for
such a meritorious act.

00:04:26.291 --> 00:04:30.261
Right. Does saying that mean you
want to go and accept the medal?

00:04:30.261 --> 00:04:30.662
Aye, sir!

00:04:30.662 --> 00:04:31.996
Until we complete repairs...

00:04:31.996 --> 00:04:33.930
...it isn't wise to move the ship.

00:04:34.065 --> 00:04:36.659
Oh, that's okay. We'll take the Galileo.

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.230
Take the Galileo?

00:04:38.503 --> 00:04:41.199
Come on. It'll be a little
one-hour rendezvous.

00:04:41.339 --> 00:04:42.499
You can go by yourself.

00:04:43.341 --> 00:04:44.501
Wanna come, Mr. Yamamoto?

00:04:44.776 --> 00:04:48.610
Me, sir? Yes! I'd be glad to!

00:04:48.813 --> 00:04:49.939
If the captain leaves the ship...

00:04:50.014 --> 00:04:53.279
...the first officer must remain
to take responsibility for it.

00:04:55.286 --> 00:04:58.949
Good point. Going with a another
guy wouldn't be any fun.

00:05:00.024 --> 00:05:02.322
That's not what I'm saying!

00:05:02.627 --> 00:05:04.595
How about you, Miss Kim?

00:05:05.797 --> 00:05:06.564
Come on, Mr. Katori!

00:05:06.564 --> 00:05:06.698
Um...
Come on, Mr. Katori!

00:05:06.698 --> 00:05:07.098
Um...

00:05:07.098 --> 00:05:10.556
I'm sure there're be plenty
of great food at the party.

00:05:10.635 --> 00:05:12.296
Everyone's busy!

00:05:12.704 --> 00:05:15.138
That's right... Oh, yeah!

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:16.734
That's what I'll do!

00:05:17.308 --> 00:05:20.937
Don't worry! I'll bring you
all back a doggie bag!

00:05:26.651 --> 00:05:29.313
A young guy shouldn't act so weak!

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:34.415
Okay, all disinfected!

00:05:35.059 --> 00:05:37.323
Okay, now it's your turn!

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:40.357
Stop it! Please!

00:05:43.401 --> 00:05:45.136
The Raalgon Empire won't let...

00:05:45.136 --> 00:05:47.900
...Admiral Donan's death go unpunished.

00:05:48.406 --> 00:05:50.772
The time for me to fulfill my
mission is drawing near.

00:05:53.912 --> 00:05:54.844
Harumi.

00:05:56.047 --> 00:05:57.309
Harumi!

00:05:58.683 --> 00:05:59.741
Harumi!

00:06:01.085 --> 00:06:01.642
Yes?

00:06:01.886 --> 00:06:04.912
It's not like you to be
so absent-minded.

00:06:04.989 --> 00:06:08.117
No, I'm okay. Prepare an IV, right?

00:06:08.726 --> 00:06:09.827
Want an IV?

00:06:09.827 --> 00:06:10.885
Uh-uh!

00:06:11.095 --> 00:06:13.359
Then get me the antibiotics so
I can stop his infection.

00:06:13.431 --> 00:06:14.159
Right.

00:06:14.432 --> 00:06:17.629
Being a soldier doesn't mean
you aren't human. Get some rest.

00:06:18.236 --> 00:06:20.329
Absent-minded? Me?

00:06:20.705 --> 00:06:23.401
Did someone program that into
my psychological system?

00:06:32.116 --> 00:06:34.380
Hey, the Galileo's hatch is opening.

00:06:35.119 --> 00:06:38.520
But we're not done fixing it.
What's going on?

00:06:38.623 --> 00:06:41.148
Harumi? You got those
antibiotics for me yet?

00:06:42.126 --> 00:06:43.320
Harumi?

00:06:49.734 --> 00:06:50.928
Wasn't that with him?!

00:06:51.469 --> 00:06:52.595
Harumi!

00:06:53.137 --> 00:06:55.367
The captain took Harumi with him?

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.071
What's the deal?!

00:06:57.241 --> 00:06:59.869
It's your fault for letting him
run wild on the ship!

00:07:00.478 --> 00:07:03.879
She'll never make it back
alive alone with him!

00:07:04.148 --> 00:07:05.080
It's possible.

00:07:05.149 --> 00:07:06.173
What?!

00:07:09.487 --> 00:07:12.217
So, what's this "secret mission" of ours?

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.390
Just wait till we get there.

00:07:15.159 --> 00:07:18.356
We didn't tell the doctor.
Isn't this a little suspicious?

00:07:18.596 --> 00:07:24.398
Suspicious? What, have those
rumors about us spread that much?

00:07:24.836 --> 00:07:26.804
Man, this could cause trouble.

00:07:27.171 --> 00:07:31.733
I'd intended to share my love equally
with all the girls on board.

00:07:31.876 --> 00:07:32.900
That's not what I meant.

00:07:34.178 --> 00:07:36.976
I just don't understand you, sir.

00:07:37.181 --> 00:07:38.739
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:07:38.816 --> 00:07:41.114
Being upset and worried never helps.

00:07:41.185 --> 00:07:43.847
If you have a life, you may as well enjoy it!

00:07:47.525 --> 00:07:51.120
Oh, have to report in?
Don't mind me. Go ahead.

00:07:51.195 --> 00:07:52.787
But, right now...

00:07:52.997 --> 00:07:56.728
If you're afraid I'll listen, I'll plug
my ears and shut my eyes.

00:07:56.834 --> 00:07:57.823
Go on. It's okay.

00:07:58.202 --> 00:08:00.534
Um, it's stopped.

00:08:00.738 --> 00:08:02.706
Is that okay? Won't they get mad?

00:08:03.541 --> 00:08:05.168
I thought you couldn't hear me.

00:08:06.177 --> 00:08:09.635
Huh? What's that?
I can't hear you. Not a word!

00:08:11.549 --> 00:08:13.676
Can't hear a single thing!

00:08:19.223 --> 00:08:20.713
You can't reach her?

00:08:20.792 --> 00:08:25.161
No, ma'am. From our last contact point,
we calculate she's nearby.

00:08:25.329 --> 00:08:27.763
Search! The Soyokaze must be
around here somewhere!

00:08:27.832 --> 00:08:28.355
Aye, aye!

00:08:30.735 --> 00:08:34.000
They're around here. They're somewhere close.

00:08:34.539 --> 00:08:36.370
There has to be a way to contact her!

00:08:37.408 --> 00:08:40.309
Don't you people understand
the pure hearts men have?!

00:08:40.578 --> 00:08:42.910
I've got a major problem with this!

00:08:43.247 --> 00:08:45.374
Not just you! Both of us!

00:08:45.583 --> 00:08:48.677
The major problem is getting
the ship repaired quickly!

00:08:48.753 --> 00:08:50.778
If anything happens to Harumi...

00:08:50.888 --> 00:08:52.753
...then we'll make that idiot pay!

00:08:53.091 --> 00:08:53.853
Hold it a sec!

00:08:53.958 --> 00:08:55.357
What's wrong, Kim?

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.126
I'm reading Raalgon transmissions.
They're close!

00:08:58.563 --> 00:09:00.724
Can you pinpoint them?

00:09:00.865 --> 00:09:03.527
Gas jamming in the area is preventing it.

00:09:03.601 --> 00:09:04.502
What?!

00:09:04.502 --> 00:09:05.230
Engine room!

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:07.470
Do we have our main guns back on line?

00:09:07.605 --> 00:09:09.038
Give us a little more time.

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:13.208
That red giant's heat overloaded
our energy systems.

00:09:13.277 --> 00:09:15.837
If we activate them now,
we risk blowing the whole ship!

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:17.112
How much longer?

00:09:17.281 --> 00:09:19.215
Give it at least two hours.

00:09:19.617 --> 00:09:20.549
That long?!

00:09:20.785 --> 00:09:22.514
If we play this wrong, the captain and Harumi...

00:09:22.587 --> 00:09:24.612
...will make it out okay while we get destroyed.

00:09:24.922 --> 00:09:27.550
Wait a minute! If there's
gas jamming in the area...

00:09:27.625 --> 00:09:30.594
...then the Raalgon can't locate us, either!

00:09:30.895 --> 00:09:33.227
As long as we don't broadcast any radio signals.

00:09:33.297 --> 00:09:34.264
It's worth a try!

00:09:34.899 --> 00:09:38.027
Anyway, we'd better get the
repair crews back inside.

00:09:38.636 --> 00:09:41.696
We have to try anything to
keep from being discovered.

00:09:41.973 --> 00:09:46.433
Right! Lieutenant Andressen!
Sergeant Cryburn!

00:09:48.946 --> 00:09:50.715
Okay, you apes! Drop everything
and get back in the ship!

00:09:50.715 --> 00:09:52.383
Attention, repair crew! Emergency!
Okay, you apes! Drop everything
and get back in the ship!

00:09:52.383 --> 00:09:53.284
Attention, repair crew! Emergency!

00:09:53.284 --> 00:09:54.273
Attention, repair crew! Emergency!
Move it!

00:09:54.485 --> 00:09:55.509
Enemy ship approaching!

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:58.582
Cease all radio transmissions
and return to the ship!

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:01.623
All radio transmissions are now restricted!

00:10:03.928 --> 00:10:06.920
Why am I so uncertain now?

00:10:08.666 --> 00:10:10.600
Something wrong, Captain?

00:10:10.802 --> 00:10:12.292
Did you bring a dress?

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:14.968
A dress, sir? No.

00:10:15.339 --> 00:10:18.968
Uh-oh, and I didn't bring my new suit, either.

00:10:19.343 --> 00:10:22.437
It's a party, after all.
We should get dressed up.

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:23.274
A party?

00:10:23.481 --> 00:10:24.573
Okay, U-turn!

00:10:24.982 --> 00:10:26.244
We're going back?

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:27.749
Yup! Captain's orders!

00:10:28.319 --> 00:10:29.149
Aye, sir.

00:10:46.571 --> 00:10:49.802
Picking up enemy search radar. Very strong.

00:10:49.974 --> 00:10:52.238
All repair crews are back on board.

00:10:54.879 --> 00:10:57.279
Lieutenant, another ship is approaching us.

00:10:57.682 --> 00:10:58.614
Raalgon?

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:01.644
Hello? Anybody hear me?

00:11:02.987 --> 00:11:04.887
Ca- Captain!

00:11:05.189 --> 00:11:06.087
What's going on?!

00:11:06.224 --> 00:11:07.282
He's on the emergency channel.

00:11:07.925 --> 00:11:10.291
I was getting worried when
nobody was answering me.

00:11:10.361 --> 00:11:11.953
I forgot something, so I came back.

00:11:12.029 --> 00:11:14.759
Great! At a time like this!

00:11:15.032 --> 00:11:16.932
Lieutenant Katori, what's the Galileo's position?

00:11:17.001 --> 00:11:19.970
0010. Entering the enemy's detection area.

00:11:26.377 --> 00:11:28.845
Captain, an enemy vessel is approaching.

00:11:29.247 --> 00:11:32.546
The Soyokaze is in no condition to fight.

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:34.308
This is our final transmission.

00:11:34.685 --> 00:11:37.119
Turn and fly as far away as you can.
That is all!

00:11:38.022 --> 00:11:38.886
Lieutenant...

00:11:39.423 --> 00:11:41.948
No matter what they're like...

00:11:42.026 --> 00:11:44.392
...you shouldn't let someone die
when they might be saved!

00:11:44.695 --> 00:11:49.132
BINGO! Everyone listening?
This is a direct order.

00:11:49.734 --> 00:11:52.202
Shut down all power systems and run silent.

00:11:52.637 --> 00:11:54.104
The entire electrical
system, got that?

00:11:54.438 --> 00:11:57.100
The Soyokaze's air should last for a few hours.

00:11:57.408 --> 00:12:00.275
Once we're in the enemy's sensor area,
we'll do the same.

00:12:00.344 --> 00:12:02.107
All clear? Don't move!

00:12:02.446 --> 00:12:05.677
If anyone breaks these orders,
they'll be court-martialed! Out!

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:09.645
Sorry, Harumi, but could
you shut down all our systems?

00:12:09.754 --> 00:12:12.689
But, Captain, if we do that,
the oxygen supply will...

00:12:12.757 --> 00:12:14.224
Captain's orders.

00:12:14.325 --> 00:12:15.485
Aye, sir.

00:12:28.673 --> 00:12:30.641
I'm assuming command.

00:12:31.075 --> 00:12:33.669
Cut all power systems and run silent!

00:12:38.149 --> 00:12:42.051
You picked up the Earth ship's
transmission? Did you locate them?

00:12:42.286 --> 00:12:44.015
No, it cut out too quickly.

00:12:44.155 --> 00:12:46.385
It looks like they spotted our sensor sweep.

00:12:46.624 --> 00:12:48.455
Shall I try contacting Harumi again?

00:12:48.793 --> 00:12:49.555
No, wait!

00:12:50.127 --> 00:12:53.028
We're not in any hurry.
Take your time in searching.

00:12:53.197 --> 00:12:53.822
Aye!

00:13:00.504 --> 00:13:02.233
Ow! Who did that?!

00:13:04.108 --> 00:13:06.474
Idiot! You're wasting air!

00:13:07.511 --> 00:13:10.446
How long do you suppose
the ship's air will last?

00:13:10.614 --> 00:13:12.775
Dunno. A few hours,
if we're lucky.

00:13:13.084 --> 00:13:16.053
If they don't give up before then, it's all over.

00:13:18.422 --> 00:13:21.357
Distance to enemy vessel now 0006.

00:13:21.559 --> 00:13:25.051
Lieutenant, how long can the
air last in the Galileo?

00:13:25.129 --> 00:13:27.290
Maybe... thirty minutes.

00:13:27.865 --> 00:13:30.095
And if the enemy ship doesn't give up by then...

00:13:34.839 --> 00:13:38.798
Whoever said that space is
just a world of darkness?

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:41.376
Don't you think this
scenery looks beautiful?

00:13:41.846 --> 00:13:44.144
Why, sir? If you'd done as
Lieutenant Yamamoto said...

00:13:44.215 --> 00:13:45.682
...we would be safe.

00:13:46.083 --> 00:13:48.108
If we ran, we would have been spotted.

00:13:48.185 --> 00:13:50.119
The Raalgon are pretty smart that way.

00:13:50.388 --> 00:13:53.482
Captain, you're impressed by
your enemy's strength?

00:13:53.758 --> 00:13:55.055
There's no difference.

00:13:55.126 --> 00:13:57.822
Human or Raalgon, a strong
person is still strong.

00:13:59.563 --> 00:14:02.498
It's best not to try and resist
someone who's stronger.

00:14:02.566 --> 00:14:06.627
You're willing to sacrifice yourself
to save the Soyokaze?

00:14:09.173 --> 00:14:11.869
Yeah, that doesn't sound too bad.

00:14:12.576 --> 00:14:15.170
Besides, I get to be alone
with a beautiful woman.

00:14:15.246 --> 00:14:17.544
This situation is pretty good...

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:20.239
Captain!

00:14:25.222 --> 00:14:29.522
Guess I talked too much...
Wasted my... air...

00:14:37.935 --> 00:14:40.062
They're slowing down, which means...

00:14:40.137 --> 00:14:43.163
...they know we're here.

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:47.108
But how did they find the Soyokaze so quickly?

00:14:47.178 --> 00:14:50.011
They probably traced the
captain's final transmission.

00:14:50.181 --> 00:14:54.208
They must have longer-ranged
sensors then we have.

00:14:54.285 --> 00:14:55.877
What're they doing now?

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:56.711
Pervert!

00:14:57.521 --> 00:14:59.216
Whaddaya mean, pervert?!

00:15:00.991 --> 00:15:03.289
Their sensors are probably incredibly sensitive!

00:15:03.594 --> 00:15:05.528
They sent me to say that...

00:15:05.596 --> 00:15:07.898
...the main guns will be ready sooner
than they expected.

00:15:07.898 --> 00:15:08.887
REALLY?!

00:15:10.968 --> 00:15:15.234
Looks like cutting the power
cooled the systems faster.

00:15:15.406 --> 00:15:19.809
Wow, Tylor's orders actually
helped for a change.

00:15:20.144 --> 00:15:21.475
What about the Galileo's air?

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:24.313
Dangerously low.

00:15:27.651 --> 00:15:29.585
Captain, wake up!

00:15:30.955 --> 00:15:32.013
I'm fine.

00:15:32.957 --> 00:15:35.517
Harumi... You seem to be
holding up... pretty well...

00:15:45.903 --> 00:15:47.734
It's okay, Harumi...

00:15:48.272 --> 00:15:50.604
You must be suffering, too.

00:15:50.741 --> 00:15:52.971
Sorry I got your compact dirty.

00:15:53.277 --> 00:15:55.336
Just relax...

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.614
Why, Captain?

00:15:58.716 --> 00:15:59.774
Why what?

00:16:04.522 --> 00:16:06.956
Why are you so kind?

00:16:07.158 --> 00:16:10.025
I... I don't think I'm that kind at all...

00:16:10.661 --> 00:16:15.462
But you're like everyone else
on the Soyokaze is to me...

00:16:16.033 --> 00:16:19.628
You're my crew... and you're important to me...

00:16:19.703 --> 00:16:22.001
Your crew? Important to you?

00:16:22.606 --> 00:16:25.006
You care about me as one of your crew?

00:16:25.709 --> 00:16:26.835
Captain!

00:16:27.044 --> 00:16:31.504
I'm sorry for lying to you!
I'm not a real human!

00:16:31.715 --> 00:16:33.114
I'm an android!

00:16:33.384 --> 00:16:35.978
Oh... Really?

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:38.987
You're not angry?! After you protected me...

00:16:39.056 --> 00:16:41.524
...and I still lied to you? You're not angry?

00:16:41.725 --> 00:16:44.660
That doesn't change... who you are...

00:16:44.862 --> 00:16:45.692
Captain!

00:16:46.363 --> 00:16:49.662
Even though I'm a spy?
Even though I'm an android?

00:16:49.733 --> 00:16:52.099
It doesn't matter to me.

00:16:52.369 --> 00:16:55.668
To me, you're just... Harumi...

00:16:55.973 --> 00:16:56.962
Captain!

00:17:20.097 --> 00:17:21.121
Captain!

00:17:21.932 --> 00:17:22.990
Just go away already!

00:17:23.467 --> 00:17:26.265
Lieutenant, the Galileo can't last much longer!

00:17:27.738 --> 00:17:31.697
It's not right, leaving him to die.
Even he doesn't deserve that!

00:17:32.042 --> 00:17:35.705
Shall I take your place at the
court-martial, Lieutenant?

00:17:35.980 --> 00:17:36.708
What?

00:17:37.381 --> 00:17:39.576
Lieutenant, we have to risk it.

00:17:41.785 --> 00:17:44.310
All right! I'll accept the responsibility!

00:17:44.788 --> 00:17:47.780
All hands, prepare to move out!
Battle stations!

00:17:49.326 --> 00:17:52.591
Soyokaze spotted!
It... It's right under us!

00:17:52.663 --> 00:17:55.223
Don't panic! Battle stations!

00:17:58.669 --> 00:17:59.397
Captain!

00:18:00.804 --> 00:18:01.736
Captain...

00:18:21.358 --> 00:18:22.655
Harumi...

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:27.529
Don't worry, sir. I'll contact the
Raalgon and request a rescue.

00:18:27.831 --> 00:18:30.197
I won't let them lay a finger on you!

00:18:30.467 --> 00:18:32.094
Well, that doesn't sound so bad...

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:34.735
...but I think it's all right.

00:18:46.817 --> 00:18:48.751
Lieutenant Kim! Contact the Galileo...

00:18:49.253 --> 00:18:50.777
...and make sure the captain's all right!

00:18:51.055 --> 00:18:51.714
Aye, sir!

00:18:52.289 --> 00:18:53.924
Main guns, ready to fire!

00:18:53.924 --> 00:18:55.516
Right! Hard about!

00:18:55.759 --> 00:18:57.124
Rear cannon, ready to fire!

00:18:57.261 --> 00:18:59.320
Wait! We gain nothing by destroying it!

00:18:59.496 --> 00:19:02.260
Captain! We've lost sight of the Soyokaze!

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:03.289
What?!

00:19:11.542 --> 00:19:13.407
Enemy shuttle craft sighted!

00:19:13.477 --> 00:19:15.843
Idiot! Find me the Soyokaze!

00:19:17.114 --> 00:19:19.378
We're dead in their sights!

00:19:26.457 --> 00:19:27.788
Prepare to fire!

00:19:27.858 --> 00:19:29.849
No time! Leave this to me!

00:19:30.361 --> 00:19:31.259
WHAT?!

00:19:43.907 --> 00:19:45.807
Enemy vessel destroyed!

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:48.337
I've confirmed that the captain
and Harumi are all right.

00:19:48.412 --> 00:19:50.903
Currently en route back to the Soyokaze!

00:20:04.528 --> 00:20:05.859
Well, everyone's here.

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:09.190
How can you just say that?!
We were so worried about you!

00:20:09.266 --> 00:20:11.860
Really? You were worried about me, Yuriko!

00:20:11.935 --> 00:20:13.095
That's great!

00:20:14.905 --> 00:20:19.604
You're a total mess and Harumi
came out just fine.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.839
Well, girls can be tough, you know?

00:20:21.945 --> 00:20:25.005
I'm sorry, Doctor. Would you excuse me?

00:20:25.249 --> 00:20:28.878
You're probably tired, Harumi.
Get some rest, okay?

00:20:29.153 --> 00:20:30.814
Yuriko, help me!

00:20:32.289 --> 00:20:34.883
Well, let's start fresh with a little drink.

00:20:35.058 --> 00:20:36.855
Care to join me, Captain?

00:20:37.094 --> 00:20:37.890
Sure thing!

00:20:38.128 --> 00:20:38.856
Captain!

00:20:38.929 --> 00:20:39.486
Right...

00:20:41.965 --> 00:20:43.432
HARUMI!

00:20:44.301 --> 00:20:46.132
Harumi, are you okay?!

00:20:46.437 --> 00:20:49.668
Tylor didn't try anything with you, did he?!

00:20:49.973 --> 00:20:51.235
We'll kill him!

00:20:51.475 --> 00:20:53.636
The captain is a wonderful man.

00:20:54.077 --> 00:20:57.046
The fool you see isn't the real man.

00:20:59.483 --> 00:21:00.780
A wonderful man?

00:21:01.185 --> 00:21:02.584
Wonderful how?

00:21:09.226 --> 00:21:13.629
Anguish... Uncertainty... Tears...

00:21:22.439 --> 00:21:23.006
Yes?

00:21:23.006 --> 00:21:23.734
Harumi?

00:21:23.941 --> 00:21:24.498
Yes.

00:21:24.808 --> 00:21:26.207
Prepare to capture Tylor.

00:21:27.244 --> 00:21:30.941
What's wrong? Tylor hasn't
seduced you, has he?

00:21:31.048 --> 00:21:33.744
No! The captain would never do that!

00:21:35.352 --> 00:21:36.444
Is she?!

00:21:36.854 --> 00:21:39.982
Pardon, but are we capturing him
to be executed on the Melva?

00:21:40.424 --> 00:21:41.914
That's no concern of yours.

00:21:42.192 --> 00:21:42.920
But...

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:46.960
Fool! An android shouldn't
care about such things!

00:21:47.531 --> 00:21:49.465
An android has no use for emotions!

00:21:50.167 --> 00:21:51.566
No use for emotions!

00:21:53.637 --> 00:21:54.569
Is that clear?

00:21:55.305 --> 00:21:58.797
Begin the mission for which
you've been preparing. That is all.

00:21:59.209 --> 00:21:59.937
Acknowledged.

00:22:12.689 --> 00:22:13.656
The Irresponsible Captain Tylor
Next Episode

00:22:15.492 --> 00:22:17.427
Having a heart is a human weakness.

00:22:17.427 --> 00:22:19.418
Having a heart is a human wonder.

00:22:19.496 --> 00:22:21.225
That's what makes us wonderful.

00:22:21.398 --> 00:22:23.889
Next time, "Shiny! Happy! (Deadly) Germs."

00:22:24.034 --> 00:22:24.898
Watch for it.

00:22:25.302 --> 00:22:27.395
Filming is Job 1!
Working hard for those who demand
the finest in image and sound

00:22:38.549 --> 00:22:41.652
All he has to do is just...
Machi o Aitsu ga Aruiteru dake de

00:22:41.652 --> 00:22:44.746
...walk around downtown.
Machi o Aitsu ga Aruiteru dake de

00:22:45.255 --> 00:22:48.725
He's a playful man who catches...
Nandemo Ki o Hiku Ochame na Yatsu sa

00:22:48.725 --> 00:22:51.558
...the eyes of all who he meets.
Nandemo Ki o Hiku Ochame na Yatsu sa

00:22:52.062 --> 00:22:54.898
Oh! That's why, you see...
Aa, Dakara sa Sou Kore kara Shuyaku

00:22:54.898 --> 00:22:58.698
...he'll be our hero from now on.
Aa, Dakara sa Sou Kore kara Shuyaku

00:22:59.503 --> 00:23:01.872
So, let's begin...
Henshin Byouyomi o Shite yo!

00:23:01.872 --> 00:23:05.706
...the countdown for the change!
Henshin Byouyomi o Shite yo!

00:23:09.179 --> 00:23:11.977
Take a deep breath, and one two.
12345 Ikizugi o One Two

00:23:13.116 --> 00:23:15.452
Now stride out...
Saa Kore kara Kuridasou

00:23:15.452 --> 00:23:18.615
...with your head held high.
Saa Kore kara Kuridasou

00:23:18.755 --> 00:23:22.486
Downtown Dance
